Third-party dictionary data used by pinyindata

Sources and transformations:

* mozillazg/pinyin-data, pinyin.txt (v0.15.0)
  https://github.com/mozillazg/pinyin-data/tree/9d05c9e29cb6a7e5c79f2f5279f5c1014246a19a
  Kept Han characters and the first reading of each character; stripped tones
  and encoded ü as v. The upstream data includes readings from Unicode Unihan.

* mozillazg/phrase-pinyin-data, pinyin.txt (v0.19.0)
  https://github.com/mozillazg/phrase-pinyin-data/tree/7aac0bf2af6d448815d69399e56eca1302fd2326
  Kept Han-only entries and the first reading of repeated phrases; stripped tones.
  The separate large_pinyin.txt and cc_cedict.txt files are not used.

* zh-lx/pinyin-pro (package version 3.29.5),
  packages/pinyin-pro/lib/data/{dict1-pinyin,dict2,dict3,dict4,dict5,surname}.ts
  https://github.com/zh-lx/pinyin-pro/tree/0785234b4dc0fa3ea9f244e3d77703b2df6a9db4
  Common-character defaults, supplemental phrases and surname readings, stripped
  of tones. Common-character defaults take precedence over pinyin-data defaults.

* @pinyin-pro/data, packages/data/json/traditional.json (same revision)
  Traditional-to-simplified character mapping for phrase and surname lookup.

Generated dictionaries combine these sources and the project corrections in
  data/overrides.txt. Source revisions and SHA-256 checks are pinned in
  internal/generate/main.go. No upstream conversion implementation is copied.

The upstream MIT notices and the Unicode data notice follow in full.

